(ned ROTARY START -- park over the bar so the operator can lower the probe.)
(Operator 2026-08-12: "have it go to that XY after a click but at Ztop so user)
(can lower the probe in case its a different length probe".)

(WHY THE HEIGHT IS NOT STORED WITH THE XY. The XY of the bar does not change)
(- the fixture is bolted down - but the probe sticking out of the spindle does,)
(every time a different one goes in. So the machine owns the XY and the)
(operator owns the Z. Storing a Z here would be storing a property of a probe)
(that may not be in the spindle next time.)

(Z FIRST, THEN XY. Always: the spindle may be sitting anywhere, and a lateral)
(move at an unknown depth is how a probe gets snapped off against the bar or)
(the chuck. Going up first costs nothing and cannot hit anything.)

(NO BAR DIAMETER ANYWHERE IN THIS CHAIN. It is derived later from the two)
(flank touches and the crown, so it can never be typed in wrong.)
o<rotary_goto_start> sub
  (Arg names are the GUI binding: SubCallButton looks for a widget of the)
  (same name and falls back to the bracketed default.)
  #<rp_sx>   = #1 (=-3729.5550 bar centre X machine)
  #<rp_sy>   = #2 (=-1365.0498 bar centre Y machine)
  #<rp_ztop> = #3 (=-196.1488 park height machine)
  #<rp_ftrav> = #4 (=2000.0 traverse mm/min)
  #<sx>    = #<rp_sx>
  #<sy>    = #<rp_sy>
  #<ztop>  = #<rp_ztop>
  #<ftrav> = #<rp_ftrav>
  o1 if [#<ftrav> LE 0]
    #<ftrav> = 2000.0
  o1 endif
  o2 if [#<sx> EQ 0 AND #<sy> EQ 0]
    (abort, ROTARY START: no stored bar XY - teach it first)
  o2 endif
  o5 if [#<_metric> EQ 0]
    (abort, ROTARY START: switch to MM first)
  o5 endif
  G90
  G1 G53 Z[#<ztop>] F[#<ftrav>]
  G1 G53 X[#<sx>] Y[#<sy>] F[#<ftrav>]
  (PRINT, ROTARY START: over the bar at X#<sx> Y#<sy> machine, parked at Z#<ztop>.)
  (PRINT, NEXT: jog Z down beside the bar, below the crown, then start the probe cycle.)
o<rotary_goto_start> endsub
M2 (end program)
